Hi, Bob, no, I haven’t written this up, I’ll try to do so. There is some literature on the related problem for multiple imputation; see links here:
http://andrewgelman.com/2011/10/01/when-should-you-worry-about-imputed-data/
Currently we do mulitple imputation using mi, the difference is that it does not use iterative algorithms to draw from the conditional posteriors so we don’t have the concern of the chains not catching up to the input stream of simulations obtained from the first model.
A

