Hi Daniel and Bob,

To test 2.5.0 with Julia’s Stan.jl I did:

cd ~/Projects/Stan
Renamed  cmdstan  to cmdstan-2.4.0 (to have a backup copy is ever needed).

git clone https://github.com/stan-dev/cmdstan.git
cd cmdstan
make stan-update
make build

Worked flawlessly.

On my OSX 10.10/XCode 6 system, I also updated the makefile (switched the compiler from g++ -> clang++ and optimization level for the stan compiler from O_STANC = 0 -> O_STANC = 3).

Daniel: I did notice the cmdstan/stan/example-models dir is empty, should I perform another step? Or is that now done automatically as in below message?

Bob: A (very) minor documentation suggestion is to, on page 15 of the Reference Manual (Future Interfaces), add links to what’s available, e.g. https://github.com/goedman/Stan.jl in my case. Maybe the word ‘Future’ is a bit misleading, these are really Interfaces not maintained by the Stan-team?

Rob J. Goedman
goe...@icloud.com

